  "query_preview": "../Monday through Thursday/...\n\nContinuing to see a strong low in the southern gulf, generating\nlong term near gale to strong gale force southeast winds offshore\nof Prince of Wales Island. At this time, Monday looks the\nstrongest, with gales around 40-45 knots in the southern zones and\nup to 30 knot northerlies in the inner channels. As for\nprecipitation, expect to see multiple waves of precipitation moves\nup from the south over the panhandle. These waves of moisture will\nbe pushing through constant ridging and easterly winds aloft\ncausing warming and drying. As such, overall PoP chances are very\nuncertain, with much of the southern panhandle to Icy Strait \nkeeping between 30-70%. One interesting portion of this forecast\nthough is the possibility for mixing on the leading edge of the\nmostly rain. If it does occur, and it is fairly unlikely at this\npoint, not expecting any accumulation.",
